          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Iron deficiency anemia sits in the blood chapter. Which chapter would an underlying bleeding ulcer be coded from?",
          "answer": "An underlying bleeding ulcer, given its nature as a gastrointestinal condition, would typically be coded from Chapter 11: Diseases of the digestive system (K00-K95) of the ICD-10-CM. This is because the chronic blood loss causing conditions like iron deficiency anemia is coded from the chapter that \"owns the bleeding site,\" as stated in the document \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 3: blood, blood-forming organs and the immune mechanism.\" Additionally, \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 11: diseases of the digestive system\" notes that specific bleeding presentations, such as hematemesis, melena, and unspecified gastrointestinal hemorrhage, have categories within this chapter.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
